< p: Countercyclical Capital Buffer The Countercyclical Capital Buffer (CCyB) is an element of the Federal Reserve’s regulatory toolkit. It is a macroprudential tool designed to support lending and economic activity when economic conditions de-teriorate. It augments minimum capital requirements when there is an elevated risk of above-normal losses, thus making capital requirements countercyclical, as required by the Dodd-Frank Act. For more information, see https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/bcreg20160908b.htm.
